header='''<header><a class="brand" href="/">river<b> /</b></a><span class="header-label">ANDY SERNA · PROJECT DOCS</span><button class="mobile-menu" aria-label="Toggle project navigation" aria-expanded="false">☰</button><nav><a href="/">Projects</a><a href="/about.html">About</a><a class="git" href="https://github.com/MHRiver" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></nav></header>'''
def shell(title,body,active=''):
 side='<aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Project navigation"><div class="eyebrow">Workspace</div><a class="side-home" href="/">▦ &nbsp; Project overview</a><div class="eyebrow">Documentation</div>'
 for cat in ['Development','Infrastructure','Networking','Self-hosting','Hardware']:
  side+=f'<div class="side-group">{cat}</div>'
  for p in projects:
   if p['category']==cat: side+=f'<a class="side-project {"active" if p["slug"]==active else ""}" href="/projects/{p["slug"]}.html">{p["title"]}</a>'
 side+='<div class="side-foot">Built, broken, figured out.<br>A record of learning by doing.</div></aside>'
 return f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Andy Serna’s technical project documentation, from Python and databases to networking and home lab infrastructure."><title>{title} · River Docs</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><script src="/app.js" defer></script></head><body>{header}<div class="layout">{side}<main>{body}<footer><span>RIVER / ANDY SERNA</span><span>Learn it. Build it. Document it.</span></footer></main></div></body></html>'
icons={'Development':'&lt;/&gt;','Infrastructure':'▤','Networking':'⌘','Self-hosting':'▣','Hardware':'◇'}
cards=''
for i,p in enumerate(projects):
 cards+=f'<a class="card" href="/projects/{p["slug"]}.html" data-category="{p["category"]}" data-search="{(p["title"]+" "+" ".join(p["stack"])+" "+p["description"]).lower()}"><div class="card-top"><span class="icon">{icons[p["category"]]}</span><span class="cat">{p["category"]}</span></div><h3>{p["title"]}</h3><p>{p["description"]}</p><div class="chips">'+''.join(f'<span class="chip">{t}</span>' for t in p['stack'])+f'</div><div class="card-bottom"><span>{p["status"]}</span><span>Read documentation ↗</span></div></a>'
body='''<div class="crumb">Workspace &nbsp; / &nbsp; Project overview</div><section class="hero"><div><div class="tagline"><span class="dot"></span>THE PROJECT NOTEBOOK</div><h1>Curiosity, turned<br>into <span>working systems.</span></h1><p class="intro">I'm Andy. This is where I document what I build—from Python applications to the network and servers behind my home lab. The setup, the problems, and what I learned along the way.</p></div><div class="terminal" aria-label="Illustrative project directory"><div class="term-head"><i></i><i></i><i></i> &nbsp; andy@river ~</div><pre><em>$ ls ~/projects</em>\n├── development/\n│   └── it_inventory.py\n├── infrastructure/\n│   └── proxmox-lab/\n└── networking/\n    ├── wireguard/\n    └── pihole-unbound/\n\n<em>$ keep learning_</em></pre></div></section>'''
body+=f'<div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>{len(projects):02}</strong><span>Project write-ups</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>05</strong><span>Areas of exploration</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>01</strong><span>Always-evolving home lab</span></div></div><section><div class="section-head"><h2>Explore the projects</h2><span class="count" id="result-count">{len(projects)} PROJECTS</span></div><div class="tools"><input class="search" id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search projects or technologies…" aria-label="Search projects"><div class="filters" aria-label="Filter by category">'+''.join(f'<button class="filter {"active" if i==0 else ""}" data-filter="{c}" aria-pressed="{"true" if i==0 else "false"}">{c}</button>' for i,c in enumerate(['All','Development','Infrastructure','Networking','Self-hosting','Hardware']))+f'</div></div><div class="grid">{cards}<div class="empty" hidden>No projects match. Try another search or category.</div></div></section><div class="note">These write-ups reflect projects shared so far. Historical setups and unfinished details are labeled within each page; they are not a live inventory of running services.</div>'
(root/'index.html').write_text(shell('Project overview',body))
(root/'projects').mkdir(exist_ok=True)
for i,p in enumerate(projects):
 b=f'<article class="doc"><div class="crumb"><a href="/">Projects</a> &nbsp; / &nbsp; {p["category"]} &nbsp; / &nbsp; {p["title"]}</div><div class="tagline">{p["category"].upper()} · {p["status"].upper()}</div><h1>{p["title"]}</h1><p class="intro">{p["description"]}</p><div class="chips">'+''.join(f'<span class="chip">{s}</span>' for s in p['stack'])+'</div><h2>System at a glance</h2><div class="flow">'+'<b>→</b>'.join(f'<span>{s}</span>' for s in p['flow'])+'</div><h2>What I built</h2><ul>'+''.join(f'<li>{s}</li>' for s in p['built'])+'</ul><h2>Troubleshooting notes</h2>'+''.join(f'<section class="issue"><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></section>' for title,text in p['issues'])+'<h2>What I learned</h2><ul>'+''.join(f'<li>{s}</li>' for s in p['lessons'])+'</ul>'
 if p['repo']:b+=f'<p><a class="git" href="{p["repo"]}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View source on GitHub ↗</a></p>'
 b+='<div class="note">Documentation compiled from my project notes and shared troubleshooting history. Commands, final configuration files, and screenshots will be added as they are verified. The diagram is a simplified project overview.</div><div class="doc-nav">'
 prev=projects[i-1] if i else None;nxt=projects[i+1] if i+1<len(projects) else None
 b+=(f'<a href="/projects/{prev["slug"]}.html">← {prev["title"]}</a>' if prev else '<a href="/">← All projects</a>')+(f'<a href="/projects/{nxt["slug"]}.html">{nxt["title"]} →</a>' if nxt else '<a href="/">All projects →</a>')+'</div></article>'
 (root/'projects'/f'{p["slug"]}.html').write_text(shell(p['title'],b,p['slug']))
(root/'about.html').write_text(shell('About Andy','''<article class="doc"><div class="crumb"><a href="/">Workspace</a> / About</div><div class="tagline">THE PERSON BEHIND THE LAB</div><h1>Hi, I'm <span>Andy.</span></h1><p>I'm an NJIT student exploring systems administration, networking, and infrastructure. I learn by building something, figuring out why it breaks, and working through the fix.</p><h2>Why this notebook exists</h2><p>A working project is only part of the story. These pages keep track of the decisions, connections, and troubleshooting that make the system understandable later.</p><h2>What I work on</h2><p>My projects span Python and SQL, Linux virtual machines, managed switching, DNS, remote access, reverse proxies, and self-hosted applications. My home lab gives me a place to connect those ideas.</p><h2>What's next</h2><p>Keep refining the existing projects and their documentation. Longer-term interests include multi-server applications with messaging, databases, and recovery workflows. Those ideas are future work, separate from the builds documented here.</p><p><a class="git" href="https://github.com/MHRiver" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Find my code on GitHub ↗</a></p></article>'''))
(root/'app.js').write_text('''const toggle=document.querySelector('.mobile-menu');toggle?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const open=document.querySelector('.sidebar').classList.toggle('open');toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded',String(open))});const search=document.querySelector('#search');let category='All';function filter(){let count=0;document.querySelectorAll('.card').forEach(card=>{const match=(category==='All'||card.dataset.category===category)&&card.dataset.search.includes(search.value.toLowerCase().trim());card.hidden=!match;if(match)count++});document.querySelector('#result-count').textContent=count+' PROJECT'+(count===1?'':'S');document.querySelector('.empty').hidden=count!==0}document.querySelectorAll('.filter').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{category=button.dataset.filter;document.querySelectorAll('.filter').forEach(b=>{b.classList.toggle('active',b===button);b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button))});filter()}));search?.addEventListener('input',filter);''')
